  "summary_en": "A survey and conceptual framework for trustworthy physical intelligence. It traces failure propagation across a five-stage life cycle, introduces T-PAIO to operationalize governance in each stage, and proposes the T-PAI framework: robust and safe operation, human-centered values, integrity/privacy/equity, accountability and oversight, and sustainability.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Existing trustworthy AI frameworks, built for digital systems, miss physical safety, cyber-physical security and manufacturing concerns.",
   "Failures propagate across interdependent life cycle stages, so governance must span the whole life cycle.",
   "T-PAIO operationalizes governance elements across research, design, data, model and deployment stages.",
   "T-PAI organizes five principle groups for governing physical intelligence systems.",
   "Proposes measurable checks, e.g. a data lineage completeness metric for training provenance."
